{
  "_note": "Enemy kinds. hp and damage are multiplied by the spawn's strength factor (walls past the gate use passage.late_strength). aura_value feeds hidden latent aura on kill; remains: the item every kill of this kind leaves (Brent 2026-10-18: kills pay loot, not cash). drops: unused since the Netherecho exists - constructs are subdued there, never looted. loot: item drops left on the ground, each rolled independently. shove_resist scales how far a shove moves this enemy: 1.0 light, 0.5 heavy, 0.25 elite - never zero. design/05 step 2: poise (see balance.combat); behaviour is melee | ranged | pouncer. A melee enemy may set attack_shape 'circle' (hits everything within attack_radius of itself when the wind-up ends), interruptible (a white flash; an interrupting skill or a poise break cancels it), stuck_after_miss (seconds it stands open after hitting nothing) and front_armour (share of damage it ignores from its front arc). ranged: holds between keep_range_min and max, aims for windup seconds along a line that stops following you aim_lock seconds before release, backs off if you come within back_off_within. pouncer: circles at circle_distance; when you have been moving away from the pack for pounce_after_retreat_s it crouches for windup and leaps pounce_range; any hit during the crouch or the leap knocks it down for knockdown_s; a leap that misses leaves it stuck. STEP 4 (design/05 6.1): front_armour may be dropped below front_armour_until_frac of health; blocks_shots: a piercing shot from the front stops on it; stagger_s: how long a poise break lasts for this kind; attack_shove: metres its blow pushes the player; death_burst: what it leaves when it dies (scripts/censer_burst.gd); aura_ring: a ring drawn on the ground round it. behaviour support (the Drummer): never attacks, stands stand_behind metres behind the line, gives aura_status to allies within aura_radius, and every attack_cooldown winds up a roll (interruptible) that gives roll_status to one ally. behaviour commander: melee with a counter-swing after a blocked hit, and by health phase2_at: 'calls' reinforcements once and adds the 'sweep'; phase3_at: adds the 'charge', which crashes if it ends on a wall or stone. loot: an entry {learnable, chance} drops a skill scroll this character can learn and does not have. 2026-10-22 build: metal (0 bare, 1 mailed, 2 plated: Metal's rule, +25% a class, and Rusting burns by it), flesh (0-1, the share not under worn armour: every Disease hit and tick is multiplied by it), living (false for anything animated: Life does nothing to it), elite (the Wall Commander: holds that would lock it become something lesser). 2026-10-23 (Brent: the Stubble, unstarred first): stars - 0 for the mortal tier (design/01 LAW 2: an unstarred kill pays little latent aura, less as the star grows - balance.json 'unstarred'). creature: a procedural four-legged (or six, or two) STAND-IN model (scripts/art/creature_models.gd) until there is a creature rig source; stand_in marks them. remains may be a list (every kill leaves all of them); loot entries may carry a rarity (common | uncommon | rare) - a label, the chance is the roll. Beast behaviours (scripts/beast.gd): runner (the Gleaner - runs for the next camp, keep_away, fetch_reach), lurker (rise.*: trigger_radius, windup, radius, damage, shove; tether, burrow_s), grazer (neutral herd; charge.* as the commander's, plus max_dist and shove; angry_speed; graze_radius), flanker (flank_distance, rear_bite_mult on your back, patience_s, front_arc_deg), charger (charge.*; stuck_s after a miss), skittish (shy_radius, angry_s, calm_distance; kick.* from behind), darter (retreat_s, retreat_distance after each peck). death_burst kind 'scald' hurts whoever stands in it (scripts/scald_burst.gd); swell: below_frac of health it moves speed_mult faster.",
